BT 1 0 0 1 0 123.2 Tm /F1 8.8 Tf 12 TL (An unknown Chinese-nexus actor is running the publicly leaked DarkSword iOS exploit kit across an infrastructure of 100+ web) Tj T* (properties \(Censys\) - primarily fake AWS-console login subdomains plus Apple ID sign-in pages, hosting concentrated in Hong) Tj T* (Kong and extending to Japan, the US and Europe - to deploy the GHOSTBLADE stealer on iPhones. DarkSword is a) Tj T* (browser-to-kernel chain that strings six vulnerabilities: WebKit JavaScriptCore JIT -> PAC bypass -> sandbox escape -> kernel) Tj T* (compromise, targeting iOS 18.4 through 18.7. A malicious iframe on the lure page loads JavaScript that fires the chain; on) Tj T* (success it drops keychain/iCloud/Wi-Fi credential-dumping modules and begins a file-exfil sweep. GHOSTBLADE harvests) Tj T* (device IDs, SMS/iMessage, call history, contacts, Wi-Fi creds, Safari cookies/history, location, notes, calendar, health data,) Tj T* (photos, iCloud Drive files, emails, installed apps, saved passwords and Telegram/WhatsApp history, and specifically targets) Tj T* (exchange apps \(Coinbase, Binance, Kraken, KuCoin, OKX, MEXC\) and wallets \(Ledger, Trezor, MetaMask, Exodus, Phantom,) Tj T* (Gnosis Safe\). Promoted to Verified this run. Keep iOS fully patched \(>=18.7.x\), treat AWS/Apple login lures on unfamiliar) Tj T* (domains as hostile, and consider Lockdown Mode for high-risk staff.) Tj T* ET
