BT 1 0 0 1 0 123.2 Tm /F1 8.8 Tf 12 TL (ChainDrop, a self-propagating variant of the Shai-Hulud malware family, compromised 1,300+ package versions on npm) Tj T* (representing ~2 billion monthly downloads. Entry point: the attacker compromised the GitHub account of the maintainer behind) Tj T* (keyv, cacheable, flat-cache and file-entry-cache \(plus packages tied to Deliveroo, Ornikar, OneReach, Picsart, Qlik,) Tj T* (ServiceTitan\) and pushed malicious code to main, triggering the maintainer's own GitHub Actions pipelines to build and publish) Tj T* (infected, validly-signed versions. On npm install a hidden preinstall script \(setup.mjs\) downloads a temporary Bun runtime to) Tj T* (execute a heavily-obfuscated payload \(Math_Symbol.js\) that harvests npm publishing tokens, GitHub, cloud and infra) Tj T* (credentials from CI/CD runners and workstations, then republishes downstream packages with the payload injected - worming) Tj T* (into other maintainers' projects. It authenticates to npm, GitHub, AWS, Kubernetes and HashiCorp Vault with recovered) Tj T* (identities and uses an Ethereum dead-drop for C2 \(StepSecurity\). Response nuance \(SANS ISC #33218\): do NOT revoke the) Tj T* (stolen token first - revocation can arm the payload; scope the cleanup carefully. Pin/lock deps, block preinstall scripts in CI) Tj T* (where feasible, rotate npm/GitHub/cloud tokens, and audit for the setup.mjs/Bun/Math_Symbol.js chain.) Tj T* ET
